From: brickassembly (ISDN_Robofab)
Subject: isaacsim_rtx_compat: repin to the current Vulkan profiles package

BrickSim pins vulkan-profiles-1.4.341.0-1, which Arch has replaced with
1.4.357.0-2. The old URL 404s, so the module raised on import and the
`bricksim` CLI could not start at all.

Repinned to 1.4.357.0-2, with both SHA-256 pins recomputed. The package was
downloaded from TWO independent mirrors (geo.mirror.pkgbuild.com and
mirrors.kernel.org) and both produced the identical archive hash, so the new
pin is not "whatever one host served once".

    _PKG 149625d97130849026fb3e54acdec6b3d086f2cf35db92797f990b81c9a9cf59
    _SO  7d2d622adf83f5075a0a0ee2a16b7cbae0c508e7a0ccea15ef2478452925fa9d

NOTE: this does NOT fix the RTX segfault on this machine. With the layer
verified, extracted and all five VK_*/XDG_DATA_DIRS variables set, Isaac Sim
5.1 still crashes in librtx.scenedb.plugin.so. An identical render probe
renders 60 frames under Isaac Sim 6.0 and segfaults under 5.1 on the same
driver, so the fault is Isaac Sim 5.1, not the driver or the allocation limit
this module works around. The repin is kept because the broken download is a
real bug of its own.

Apply with: git apply ../brickassembly/patches/rtx_compat_repin.patch
---
--- /tmp/rtx.orig	2026-09-21 19:13:59.264610995 +0800
+++ BrickSim/python/isaacsim_rtx_compat.py	2026-09-21 19:13:59.269130910 +0800
@@ -41,9 +41,9 @@
